    <string name="audio_unsupported">This build\'s audio library cannot pick devices, so Android chooses them.</string>
    <string name="audio_note">Sound only ever plays to headphones; if they are unplugged the audio stops. Changing a device restarts the audio for a moment. A Bluetooth headset used as the input switches to the low-quality call mode; for the best sound use the phone or a wired mic as input and Bluetooth only for output.</string>
    <string name="mic_hint_no_wired_mic">Android sees your wired earbuds as headphones with no microphone, so their mic cannot be chosen. Unplug them and push the plug in all the way (a half-seated plug looks like plain headphones), and check that the plug has two black bands, not one. Until then, the phone\'s mic is used.</string>
    <string name="mic_hint_call">This headset\'s mic works in call mode: mono and low quality, and the sound in your ears drops to call quality too. Unless your earbuds support LE Audio, the phone\'s mic gives a much better result.</string>
    <string name="mic_hint_le">LE Audio headset: its mic should sound far better than ordinary Bluetooth call mode. If it sounds thin or muffled, switch the input back to the phone\'s mic.</string>
